## 0. Preamble

The PaperStream Permissive License (PSPL) is a permissive software license. Unlike the PaperStream License (PSL), it does **not** require derivative works to be released under an open license or their source code to be disclosed. Instead, two core conditions apply:

1. The original author or original project must be credited in every copy and every derivative work (mandatory attribution).
2. The Program, copies of it, or derivative works may **not be sold**.

This does not prevent generating revenue in other ways, such as through donations, paid support, or hosting fees (see Section 4).

This license is an independent work and is not an official GNU, MIT, or Free Software Foundation text. Because of the no-sale clause it is a source-available license, not an open source license as defined by the Open Source Initiative.

**In short:** Anyone may freely use, modify, distribute, and even embed the Program in closed-source projects. Open source is not required. The only mandatory requirements are attribution and the prohibition on selling.

